1. JWT (JSON Web Token)
What is JWT?
JWT is a token-based authentication mechanism used to securely identify users without storing session data on the server.

JWT Structure
A JWT consists of three parts:

Header.Payload.Signature
Example:

eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs...
Header
Contains algorithm information.

{
  "alg": "HS256",
  "typ": "JWT"
}
Payload
Contains user claims.

{
  "UserId": 1,
  "Name": "Pawan",
  "Role": "Admin"
}
Signature
Used to verify token authenticity.

JWT Authentication Flow
React Login Page
       |
       v
.NET Core API
       |
 Validate User
       |
 Generate JWT
       |
 Return Token
       |
React Stores Token
       |
Send Token in Authorization Header
       |
Protected API
ASP.NET Core JWT Configuration
builder.Services.AddAuthentication(JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme)
.AddJwtBearer(options =>
{
    options.TokenValidationParameters =
        new TokenValidationParameters
        {
            ValidateIssuer = true,
            ValidateAudience = true,
            ValidateLifetime = true,
            ValidateIssuerSigningKey = true
        };
});
